1
00:00:02,336 --> 00:00:04,129
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

2
00:00:04,171 --> 00:00:06,966
I REORGANIZED THE FRIDGE.

3
00:00:07,007 --> 00:00:10,886
SEE? BOTTOM SHELF:
MEATS AND DAIRY.

4
00:00:10,928 --> 00:00:14,014
MIDDLE SHELF: FRUITS
AND VEGETABLES

5
00:00:14,055 --> 00:00:18,936
AND TOP SHELF:
EXPIRED PRODUCTS.

6
00:00:18,978 --> 00:00:20,562
WHY ARE YOU DOING THIS?

7
00:00:20,604 --> 00:00:22,648
BECAUSE I AM BORED
OUT OF MY MIND.

8
00:00:22,690 --> 00:00:24,483
I'VE ALREADY BEEN
TO THE BANK

9
00:00:24,525 --> 00:00:27,026
THE POST OFFICE
AND THE DRY CLEANERS.

10
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:30,071
DUDE, YOU JUST DESCRIBED
SEVEN DAYS' WORTH OF STUFF.

11
00:00:30,113 --> 00:00:32,658
YOU GOT TO SPREAD IT OUT
A LITTLE, YOU KNOW?

12
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:34,660
HAVEN'T YOU EVER BEEN
UNEMPLOYED?

13
00:00:34,702 --> 00:00:36,119
HEY, I AM NOT UNEMPLOYED.

14
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:37,287
I'M ON SABBATICAL.

15
00:00:37,329 --> 00:00:39,206
HEY, DON'T GET
RELIGIOUS ON ME, OKAY?

16
00:00:40,833 --> 00:00:42,209
A GUY IN YOUR POSITION

17
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:43,878
NEEDS TO BE A LITTLE BETTER
AT RELAXING

18
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:44,920
YOU KNOW?

19
00:00:44,962 --> 00:00:46,171
WHY DO YOU THINK
WE HAVE

20
00:00:46,213 --> 00:00:47,715
THE COMFORTABLE
CHAIRS, HUH?

21
00:00:47,756 --> 00:00:49,717
COME HERE. SIT DOWN.

22
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:50,718
READY?

23
00:00:50,759 --> 00:00:52,093
WATCH.

24
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:54,053
AH!

25
00:00:54,095 --> 00:00:55,723
AND THEN...

26
00:00:55,764 --> 00:00:57,892
OH, YEAH! HUH?

27
00:00:57,933 --> 00:00:59,267
SO WHAT? WE JUST SIT?

28
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:00,268
OH, NO, NO.

29
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:01,770
WE'RE NOT GOING
TO JUST SIT.

30
00:01:01,812 --> 00:01:02,771
WATCH.

31
00:01:02,813 --> 00:01:03,856
( beeps )

32
00:01:05,106 --> 00:01:06,901
( phone ringing )

33
00:01:06,942 --> 00:01:08,109
Hello. Chandler Bing.

34
00:01:08,151 --> 00:01:11,196
( high voice ):
HELLO, MR. BING.

35
00:01:11,238 --> 00:01:12,447
I LOVE YOU.

36
00:01:12,489 --> 00:01:17,661
Whoever this is,
stop calling me.

37
00:01:17,703 --> 00:01:19,204
It's been six months.

38
00:01:19,246 --> 00:01:20,330
It's not funny.

39
00:01:20,372 --> 00:01:22,374
BUT I LOVE YOU.

40
00:01:22,416 --> 00:01:24,125
Leave me alone.

41
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:26,545
For the love of God,
leave me alone!

42
00:01:26,587 --> 00:01:29,088
AND THAT'S WEDNESDAY. AHH.

43
00:01:35,888 --> 00:01:40,893
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

44
00:01:40,935 --> 00:01:42,143
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

45
00:01:42,185 --> 00:01:46,189
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

46
00:01:46,231 --> 00:01:50,569
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

47
00:01:50,611 --> 00:01:52,571
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

48
00:01:52,613 --> 00:01:55,574
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

49
00:01:55,616 --> 00:01:59,244
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

50
00:01:59,286 --> 00:02:01,329
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

51
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:03,916
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

52
00:02:03,958 --> 00:02:06,167
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

53
00:02:06,209 --> 00:02:09,379
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

54
00:02:09,421 --> 00:02:11,048
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

55
00:02:19,598 --> 00:02:22,893
HEY, YOU GUYS,
GUESS WHAT.

56
00:02:22,935 --> 00:02:25,228
( bell clanging )

57
00:02:25,270 --> 00:02:26,814
THE BRITISH ARE COMING?

58
00:02:28,231 --> 00:02:30,567
OH, YOU AND YOUR WAYS.

59
00:02:32,027 --> 00:02:34,237
SINCE IT'S CHRISTMASTIME,
I'M GOING TO BE

60
00:02:34,279 --> 00:02:36,490
ONE OF THOSE PEOPLE
COLLECTING DONATIONS.

61
00:02:36,531 --> 00:02:38,117
YEAH. I ALREADY HAVE
MY BELL

62
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:39,994
AND LATER ON, I GET MY BUCKET.

63
00:02:40,035 --> 00:02:41,829
YEAH. YEAH.

64
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:44,164
I'M GOING TO BE OUT THERE
SPREADING JOY TO THE PEOPLE.

65
00:02:44,205 --> 00:02:46,416
I MEAN, LAST YEAR,
I SPREAD A LITTLE JOY

66
00:02:46,458 --> 00:02:47,876
BUT NOT REALLY ENOUGH

67
00:02:47,918 --> 00:02:50,211
SO THIS YEAR, I'M GOING
TO DO THE WHOLE CITY.

68
00:02:51,672 --> 00:02:52,881
YOU KNOW, I KNEW
A GIRL IN HIGH SCHOOL

69
00:02:52,923 --> 00:02:54,883
THAT DID THAT.

70
00:02:54,925 --> 00:02:56,426
SHE WAS VERY POPULAR.

71
00:02:56,468 --> 00:02:59,847
SO, PHEEBS, WHERE ARE YOU
DOING ALL YOUR BELL RINGING?

72
00:02:59,888 --> 00:03:02,850
THEY GAVE ME A GREAT SPOT
RIGHT BY MACY'S.

73
00:03:02,891 --> 00:03:05,686
YEAH, THEY HARDLY EVER GIVE
SUCH A GOOD CORNER TO A ROOKIE

74
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:07,228
BUT I'M THE ONLY ONE

75
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:08,981
WHO CAN SAY "MERRY CHRISTMAS"
IN 25 LANGUAGES.

76
00:03:09,023 --> 00:03:11,817
I LIED.

77
00:03:11,859 --> 00:03:12,985
OH, MY GOD.

78
00:03:13,027 --> 00:03:14,611
OKAY, YOU GUYS,
HERE'S DANNY. WATCH.

79
00:03:14,653 --> 00:03:16,030
JUST WATCH THIS.

80
00:03:19,366 --> 00:03:20,659
SEE?

81
00:03:20,701 --> 00:03:23,578
STILL PRETENDING
HE'S NOT INTERESTED.

82
00:03:24,663 --> 00:03:25,873
OKAY, HE'S COMING OVER.

83
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:27,457
JUST PRETEND
LIKE WE DON'T KNOW HIM.

84
00:03:27,499 --> 00:03:28,750
WE'VE FORGOTTEN WHO HE IS.

85
00:03:28,792 --> 00:03:29,793
HEY, GUYS.

86
00:03:29,835 --> 00:03:30,544
All:
HEY, DANNY.

87
00:03:32,546 --> 00:03:33,672
OH, DANNY, HEY.

88
00:03:33,714 --> 00:03:35,465
WHEN DID YOU
GET HERE?

89
00:03:35,507 --> 00:03:37,216
OH, GOD.

90
00:03:37,258 --> 00:03:38,468
DANNY, YOU KNOW RACHEL.

91
00:03:38,510 --> 00:03:39,553
SHE'S NICE.

92
00:03:39,594 --> 00:03:40,971
SHE'S NOT BAD
TO LOOK AT, RIGHT?

93
00:03:41,013 --> 00:03:42,305
THANKS, MON.

94
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:44,183
WELL, OF COURSE.

95
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:45,976
DO YOU WANT TO GO OUT
ON A DATE WITH HER?

96
00:03:46,018 --> 00:03:47,186
MONICA!

97
00:03:48,395 --> 00:03:49,437
ABSOLUTELY.

98
00:03:49,479 --> 00:03:50,939
IS FRIDAY OKAY?

99
00:03:52,566 --> 00:03:54,943
FRIDAY IS PERFECT.
SHE CAN'T WAIT.

100
00:03:54,985 --> 00:03:56,319
ON THE DATE,
I WILL BE ABLE

101
00:03:56,361 --> 00:03:58,030
TO TALK TO HER
DIRECTLY, RIGHT?

102
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:04,327
OKAY, WHAT THE HELL WAS THAT?

103
00:04:04,369 --> 00:04:05,328
YOU KNOW WHAT?

104
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:06,329
DON'T ANSWER ME.

105
00:04:06,371 --> 00:04:08,665
I HAVE A DATE WITH DANNY.

106
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:14,462
HOW COULD I NOT
GET THE PART?

107
00:04:14,504 --> 00:04:16,506
THE PLAY WAS ABOUT
A 29-YEAR-OLD

108
00:04:16,548 --> 00:04:18,175
ITALIAN ACTOR
FROM QUEENS.

109
00:04:18,217 --> 00:04:21,386
WELL, TALIA SHIRE SUDDENLY
BECAME AVAILABLE.

110
00:04:21,428 --> 00:04:23,680
SHE'S A WOMAN.

111
00:04:23,722 --> 00:04:25,015
WHAT CAN I SAY?

112
00:04:25,057 --> 00:04:26,808
SHE NAILED IT.

113
00:04:26,850 --> 00:04:31,188
OKAY. IS THERE
ANYTHING ELSE?

114
00:04:31,230 --> 00:04:33,899
WELL, YOU'RE JUST GOING
TO SAY NO AGAIN

115
00:04:33,941 --> 00:04:35,400
BUT GAY PORN?

116
00:04:37,903 --> 00:04:39,905
HAPPY HOLIDAYS!

117
00:04:39,947 --> 00:04:42,032
FELIZ NAVIDAD!

118
00:04:42,074 --> 00:04:45,119
ALLO AND MERRY CHRISTMAS.

119
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,327
OH, THANK YOU, SIR.

120
00:04:46,369 --> 00:04:48,538
HERE'S SOME JOY.

121
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:49,706
PHOEBE!
HEY!

122
00:04:49,748 --> 00:04:51,625
I JUST WANTED TO SEE
HOW IT'S GOING.

123
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:52,960
WELL, IT'S GOING OKAY.

124
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:55,087
WELL, GOOD.
HERE, LET ME HELP YOU OUT.

125
00:04:55,129 --> 00:04:56,713
OH, THANKS.
YEAH.

126
00:04:56,755 --> 00:04:57,756
WOW.

127
00:04:59,424 --> 00:05:00,675
IS THAT A NEW
SUEDE JACKET?

128
00:05:00,717 --> 00:05:01,969
IT LOOKS REALLY EXPENSIVE.

129
00:05:03,637 --> 00:05:06,181
YEAH... I GUESS.

130
00:05:08,642 --> 00:05:10,644
JUST GET YOUR NAILS DONE?

131
00:05:10,685 --> 00:05:13,730
YES, PHOEBE, BUT THIS IS
ALL I HAVE, OKAY?

132
00:05:13,772 --> 00:05:14,731
OKAY. THANKS.

133
00:05:14,773 --> 00:05:15,857
HAPPY HOLIDAYS.

134
00:05:15,899 --> 00:05:16,900
HERE'S YOUR JOY.

135
00:05:16,942 --> 00:05:18,568
THANK YOU.

136
00:05:18,610 --> 00:05:19,653
THANK YOU.

137
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:21,320
HAPPY HOLIDAYS.

138
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:22,990
WAIT. YOU CAN'T TAKE
THE MONEY OUT.

139
00:05:23,031 --> 00:05:23,991
I'M MAKING CHANGE.

140
00:05:24,032 --> 00:05:25,159
I NEED CHANGE FOR THE BUS.

141
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:26,660
BUT CAN'T YOU LEAVE THE DOLLAR?

142
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:27,953
THIS MONEY'S FOR THE POOR.

143
00:05:27,995 --> 00:05:30,538
I'M POOR. I GOT
TO TAKE THE BUS.

144
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:33,583
OKAY. SEASON'S GREETINGS
AND EVERYTHING, BUT STILL...

145
00:05:33,625 --> 00:05:35,002
BITE ME, BLONDIE.

146
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:36,128
OH!

147
00:05:36,170 --> 00:05:37,838
WOW.

148
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:40,924
OH, I'M GOING TO GIVE HIM
SOMETHING BESIDES JOY.

149
00:05:40,966 --> 00:05:42,550
JUST...

150
00:05:46,054 --> 00:05:47,430
THAT PART WAS
PERFECT FOR ME.

151
00:05:47,472 --> 00:05:49,016
I CAN'T BELIEVE
I DIDN'T GET IT.

152
00:05:49,057 --> 00:05:51,434
I'M SORRY, MAN.

153
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:53,645
YOU KNOW WHAT
YOU SHOULD DO?

154
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:57,232
YOU SHOULD MAKE SOMETHING HAPPEN
FOR YOURSELF, YOU KNOW?

155
00:05:57,274 --> 00:05:58,859
LIKE, LIKE WRITE A PLAY.

156
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,527
WRITE A MOVIE, HUH?

157
00:06:00,568 --> 00:06:02,529
WHAT ABOUT THOSE
GOOD WILL HUNTING GUYS?

158
00:06:02,570 --> 00:06:03,530
COME ON, ROSS

159
00:06:03,571 --> 00:06:05,073
BE REALISTIC, YOU KNOW?

160
00:06:05,115 --> 00:06:06,783
IF I DID WRITE SOMETHING

161
00:06:06,825 --> 00:06:10,537
WHAT ARE THE CHANCES I COULD GET
THOSE GUYS TO STAR IN IT?

162
00:06:13,332 --> 00:06:14,291
WAIT A SECOND.

163
00:06:14,333 --> 00:06:15,667
I COULD STAR IN IT.

164
00:06:15,709 --> 00:06:16,918
OR THAT.

165
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:20,463
I CAN'T WRITE, YOU KNOW.

166
00:06:20,505 --> 00:06:21,965
I'M AN ACTOR.

167
00:06:22,007 --> 00:06:24,759
I DON'T HAVE THE DISCIPLINE
THAT IT TAKES, YOU KNOW?

168
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:25,760
I CAN'T DO IT.

169
00:06:25,802 --> 00:06:26,887
I'LL HELP YOU.

170
00:06:26,928 --> 00:06:29,223
YEAH. I'LL MAKE
UP A SCHEDULE

171
00:06:29,264 --> 00:06:31,641
AND MAKE SURE
YOU STICK TO IT.

172
00:06:31,683 --> 00:06:33,894
PLUS IT WILL GIVE ME
SOMETHING TO DO.

173
00:06:33,935 --> 00:06:35,062
YOU'D DO THAT FOR ME?

174
00:06:35,103 --> 00:06:36,063
YEAH.

175
00:06:36,104 --> 00:06:37,147
THANKS.

176
00:06:37,189 --> 00:06:38,940
ALL RIGHT. WE'LL
START OFF SLOW.

177
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:40,817
THE ONLY THING YOU HAVE
TO DO TONIGHT

178
00:06:40,859 --> 00:06:43,278
IS COME UP WITH THE NAME
OF YOUR MAIN CHARACTER.

179
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:44,279
DONE.

180
00:06:44,321 --> 00:06:45,739
AND IT CAN'T BE JOEY.

181
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:46,656
IT'S NOT.

182
00:06:46,698 --> 00:06:47,574
OR JOSEPH.

183
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:49,659
OH.

184
00:06:53,412 --> 00:06:54,413
HI.

185
00:06:54,455 --> 00:06:55,874
WHAT'S UP?

186
00:06:55,916 --> 00:06:59,044
I JUST SAW DANNY GETTING
ON THE SUBWAY WITH A GIRL

187
00:06:59,086 --> 00:07:01,004
AND HE HAD HIS ARM
AROUND HER.

188
00:07:01,046 --> 00:07:02,589
I'M SORRY.

189
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:03,757
WELL, YOU SHOULD BE.

190
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:05,133
THIS IS ALL YOUR FAULT.

191
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:09,679
YOU MEDDLED
IN OUR RELATIONSHIP.

192
00:07:09,721 --> 00:07:11,639
YOU HAD NO RELATIONSHIP.

193
00:07:11,681 --> 00:07:13,474
NO, BUT I WAS
DOING MY THING

194
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:16,644
AND EVERYTHING WAS
GOING ACCORDING TO THE PLAN.

195
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:20,315
OH, GOD, STOP WITH THE PLAN.

196
00:07:20,357 --> 00:07:23,484
SO WHAT? SO WHAT IF YOU SAW
HIM WITH A GIRL.

197
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:25,195
WHO CARES? IT DOESN'T
MEAN ANYTHING.

198
00:07:25,237 --> 00:07:26,238
LOOK, YOU'RE GOING

199
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,781
TO GO OUT ON A
DATE WITH DANNY

200
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:29,283
AND YOU'RE GOING
TO BE SO CHARMING

201
00:07:29,324 --> 00:07:31,659
HE'S GOING TO FORGET ABOUT
THAT STUPID SUBWAY GIRL.

202
00:07:31,701 --> 00:07:35,247
SHE WAS KIND OF STUPID.

203
00:07:35,289 --> 00:07:36,581
YOU'RE RIGHT.

204
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:39,042
ALL RIGHT. I'M JUST GOING
TO GO ON THE DATE.

205
00:07:39,084 --> 00:07:41,002
I'M JUST GOING
TO GO ON THE DATE.

206
00:07:41,044 --> 00:07:43,255
THAT IS THE NEW PLAN.

207
00:07:44,923 --> 00:07:46,883
HURRY! HURRY!

208
00:08:01,815 --> 00:08:03,900
HEY, HOW DO YOU SPELL
SUSPICIOUS?

209
00:08:03,942 --> 00:08:05,360
WHY?

210
00:08:05,402 --> 00:08:07,946
BECAUSE I THINK
THIS CHARACTER IS GOING

211
00:08:07,988 --> 00:08:09,906
TO BE SUSPICIOUS ABOUT STUFF.

212
00:08:09,948 --> 00:08:11,699
YES!

213
00:08:12,993 --> 00:08:16,997
CHANDLER BING, SEVEN,
CHANDLER BING, ZERO.

214
00:08:17,038 --> 00:08:19,166
YOU'RE DRIVING
ME CRAZY WITH THAT.

215
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:20,167
OKAY. I'LL STOP.

216
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:21,168
DON'T STOP.

217
00:08:21,209 --> 00:08:22,461
MOVE THE BALL FURTHER AWAY.

218
00:08:22,501 --> 00:08:23,795
ROSS COULD MAKE THAT SHOT.

219
00:08:30,051 --> 00:08:33,930
WELL, YOU SUCK, BUT AT LEAST
YOU SUCK AT A MAN'S GAME NOW.

220
00:08:33,972 --> 00:08:35,056
YOU WANT TO PLAY?

221
00:08:35,098 --> 00:08:37,017
CHANDLER, I CAN'T BE
PLAYING GAMES.

222
00:08:37,058 --> 00:08:38,477
ROSS IS GOING
TO BE HOME SOON

223
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:40,395
AND I HAVE TO WRITE
FIVE WHOLE PAGES

224
00:08:40,437 --> 00:08:42,356
IF I'M GOING TO STICK
TO HIS SCHEDULE.

225
00:08:42,397 --> 00:08:43,690
PLAY FOR THE NEXT 30 MINUTES

226
00:08:43,731 --> 00:08:45,359
AND YOU CAN WRITE
UNTIL HE GETS HOME.

227
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:46,651
ALL RIGHT.

228
00:08:46,693 --> 00:08:50,113
BUT LISTEN,
WHAT DO YOU SAY

229
00:08:50,155 --> 00:08:53,033
WE CRANK IT
UP A NOTCH?

230
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:54,451
I'M INTRIGUED.

231
00:08:54,493 --> 00:08:57,204
ALL RIGHT. ALL WE NEED
IS A LITTLE LIGHTER FLUID.

232
00:08:57,245 --> 00:08:58,663
OKAY, BUT BE
CAREFUL, OKAY?

233
00:08:58,705 --> 00:08:59,873
BECAUSE I WANT TO GET

234
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:01,624
OUR SECURITY DEPOSIT BACK.

235
00:09:01,666 --> 00:09:03,543
YEAH, I THINK
WE SAID GOOD-BYE TO THAT

236
00:09:03,584 --> 00:09:05,086
WHEN WE INVENTED HAMMER DARTS.

237
00:09:05,128 --> 00:09:06,545
YEAH, THAT'S RIGHT.

238
00:09:06,587 --> 00:09:08,465
DO YOU REMEMBER WHICH PART
IS NOT SPACKLED?

239
00:09:08,507 --> 00:09:10,925
YEAH, RIGHT HERE.

240
00:09:13,887 --> 00:09:15,055
OH, THANK YOU.

241
00:09:15,096 --> 00:09:16,431
HAPPY HOLIDAYS.

242
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:21,228
NO, THAT'S TRASH,
YOUNG LADY.

243
00:09:21,269 --> 00:09:22,687
NO. YOU CAN'T...

244
00:09:22,729 --> 00:09:25,065
HEY, STOP THAT YOUNG LADY!

245
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:26,691
SHE DONATED TRASH!

246
00:09:26,733 --> 00:09:29,903
HEY!

247
00:09:29,944 --> 00:09:32,113
THE CHARITY'S ON FIRE!

248
00:09:32,155 --> 00:09:33,114
HELP! OH, GOOD.

249
00:09:33,156 --> 00:09:34,741
THANK YOU. I NEED THAT.

250
00:09:34,782 --> 00:09:37,118
WOO! WHAT IS THIS?

251
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:41,206
IT'S 9:00 IN THE MORNING.

252
00:09:41,248 --> 00:09:42,874
ALL RIGHT.

253
00:09:42,916 --> 00:09:44,334
"A ROOM.

254
00:09:44,376 --> 00:09:45,626
"A MAN ENTERS.

255
00:09:45,668 --> 00:09:47,128
HE LOOKS SUSPICIOUS."

256
00:09:51,716 --> 00:09:52,717
THAT'S IT?

257
00:09:54,969 --> 00:09:57,931
JOEY, YOU'RE SUPPOSED TO HAVE
FIVE PAGES DONE BY NOW

258
00:09:57,972 --> 00:09:59,807
INCLUDING AN EXCITING INCIDENT.

259
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:01,642
WHAT IS ALL THIS?

260
00:10:01,684 --> 00:10:06,440
"THE OFFICIAL RULE BOOK
OF FIREBALL."

261
00:10:06,481 --> 00:10:09,276
YEAH, THAT'S THE GAME
WE WERE PLAYING.

262
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:11,278
OH, YEAH, GREAT. SEE,
YOU TAKE A TENNIS BALL

263
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:13,029
A BOWL AND LIGHTER FLUID...

264
00:10:13,071 --> 00:10:14,822
OOPS.

265
00:10:16,657 --> 00:10:18,368
THIS IS HELPING
YOUR CAREER?

266
00:10:18,410 --> 00:10:20,287
I THOUGHT YOU WANTED
TO BE AN ACTOR.

267
00:10:20,328 --> 00:10:23,081
NOT THE CREATOR
OF "CRAZY LAWSUIT GAME."

268
00:10:23,123 --> 00:10:25,125
YOU'RE RIGHT.
YOU'RE RIGHT.

269
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:26,709
I'LL GET BACK
TO WORK.

270
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:27,710
AND SHAME ON YOU.

271
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:29,087
YOU SHOULD KNOW BETTER.

272
00:10:29,129 --> 00:10:30,213
JOEY NEEDS TO WORK.

273
00:10:30,255 --> 00:10:31,214
NOW, COME ON.

274
00:10:31,256 --> 00:10:32,257
HEY.

275
00:10:32,299 --> 00:10:34,342
UH-UH. YOU CAN HAVE
THIS BACK

276
00:10:34,384 --> 00:10:36,553
WHEN THE FIVE PAGES
ARE DONE, HUH?

277
00:10:36,595 --> 00:10:38,472
AH!

278
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:50,609
I HAD A REALLY NICE TIME
TONIGHT.

279
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:51,776
SO DID I.

280
00:10:51,818 --> 00:10:54,862
I'M REALLY GLAD
MONICA ASKED US OUT.

281
00:11:03,371 --> 00:11:05,206
I'D LOVE TO ASK
YOU IN, BUT, UH...

282
00:11:05,248 --> 00:11:06,416
MY SISTER'S VISITING

283
00:11:06,458 --> 00:11:08,460
AND I THINK SHE'S ASLEEP
ON THE COUCH.

284
00:11:08,502 --> 00:11:09,586
YOUR SISTER?

285
00:11:09,628 --> 00:11:12,172
YOUR SISTER'S ASLEEP
ON THE COUCH?

286
00:11:12,213 --> 00:11:15,049
OH, I SAW YOU WITH HER
ON THE SUBWAY

287
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:17,802
AND NOW SHE'S ASLEEP
ON THE COUCH.

288
00:11:17,844 --> 00:11:18,845
OH, GOD!

289
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:20,721
OH, I THOUGHT I HEARD YOU.

290
00:11:20,763 --> 00:11:22,349
HEY, GREAT, YOU'RE UP.

291
00:11:22,390 --> 00:11:23,975
RACHEL, THIS IS MY SISTER,
KRISTA.

292
00:11:24,017 --> 00:11:25,101
KRISTA, THIS IS RACHEL.

293
00:11:25,143 --> 00:11:26,394
HI.
NICE TO MEET YOU.

294
00:11:26,436 --> 00:11:28,021
I WISH YOU TOLD ME
WE WERE HAVING COMPANY.

295
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:29,189
I'D HAVE FIXED
MYSELF UP.

296
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:30,773
LIKE IT WOULD HELP.

297
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:32,025
YOU ARE SO BAD.

298
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:33,067
YOU ARE.

299
00:11:33,109 --> 00:11:34,194
YOU ARE.
YOU ARE.

300
00:11:34,235 --> 00:11:35,320
YOU ARE.
YOU ARE.

301
00:11:35,362 --> 00:11:36,321
YOU ARE!

302
00:11:36,363 --> 00:11:37,531
YOU ARE SO DEAD.

303
00:11:37,572 --> 00:11:38,865
I'M GOING TO GET YOU.

304
00:11:38,906 --> 00:11:39,949
( squeals )

305
00:11:39,991 --> 00:11:41,909
COME HERE!
COME HERE!

306
00:11:41,951 --> 00:11:43,870
( both laughing )

307
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:50,627
UM, VERY NICE TO MEET YOU.

308
00:11:55,048 --> 00:11:57,925
NOBODY... NOBODY
RESPECTS THE BUCKET.

309
00:11:57,967 --> 00:12:00,845
YOU WOULDN'T BELIEVE
WHAT PEOPLE PUT IN HERE.

310
00:12:00,887 --> 00:12:03,764
OKAY. DOES THIS LOOK
LIKE A GARBAGE CAN TO YOU?

311
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:05,016
NO.

312
00:12:05,058 --> 00:12:06,601
DOES IT LOOK LIKE AN ASHTRAY?

313
00:12:06,643 --> 00:12:07,602
NO.

314
00:12:07,644 --> 00:12:08,936
DOES IT LOOK LIKE A URINAL?

315
00:12:08,978 --> 00:12:11,398
EWW!

316
00:12:11,439 --> 00:12:13,149
PHEEBS, YOU GOING
TO GO BACK OUT THERE?

317
00:12:13,191 --> 00:12:14,693
WELL, YEAH.

318
00:12:14,733 --> 00:12:16,986
BUT I'M NOT GOING TO TAKE
ANY MORE CRAP, OKAY?

319
00:12:17,028 --> 00:12:18,697
NO MORE MRS. NICE BUCKET.

320
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,740
GOOD FOR YOU.
YOU'RE TOUGH.

321
00:12:21,782 --> 00:12:23,159
YOU LIVED
ON THE STREET.

322
00:12:23,201 --> 00:12:25,579
I'M GOING TO GO BACK
TO BEING STREET PHOEBE.

323
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:26,996
YEAH.

324
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:29,082
OH, BUT YOU KNOW WHAT,
I CAN'T GO TOTALLY BACK

325
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:31,167
BECAUSE STREET PHOEBE
REALLY WOULDN'T BE FRIENDS

326
00:12:31,209 --> 00:12:32,293
WITH YOU GUYS.

327
00:12:34,295 --> 00:12:37,882
HI. UM, CAN I ASK
YOU GUYS SOMETHING?

328
00:12:37,924 --> 00:12:39,342
Both:
SURE.

329
00:12:39,384 --> 00:12:41,261
UM, I DON'T HAVE
ANY BROTHERS,
SO I DON'T KNOW

330
00:12:41,302 --> 00:12:43,430
BUT DID YOU GUYS WRESTLE?

331
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:44,431
OH, YEAH.

332
00:12:44,472 --> 00:12:45,473
ALL THE TIME.

333
00:12:45,515 --> 00:12:48,935
IN FACT, I WAS
UNDEFEATED.

334
00:12:48,976 --> 00:12:51,730
WELL, YOU WEIGHED 200 POUNDS.

335
00:12:53,690 --> 00:12:55,774
STILL, I WAS
QUICK AS A CAT.

336
00:12:57,444 --> 00:12:59,862
WELL, I MET DANNY'S SISTER
YESTERDAY--

337
00:12:59,904 --> 00:13:02,907
UH, THAT WAS ACTUALLY
THE GIRL ON THE SUBWAY--

338
00:13:02,949 --> 00:13:05,702
AND, UH, YEAH,
THEY WERE VERY, YOU KNOW...

339
00:13:05,744 --> 00:13:07,078
WRESTLE-Y...

340
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,787
BUT I GUESS THAT'S NORMAL?

341
00:13:08,829 --> 00:13:11,750
WE DON'T... WE
DON'T WRESTLE NOW.

342
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:15,962
NOT SINCE I GOT TOO STRONG
FOR YOU.

343
00:13:17,338 --> 00:13:18,548
TOO STRONG FOR ME?

344
00:13:18,590 --> 00:13:19,840
YEAH.

345
00:13:19,882 --> 00:13:22,009
YOU WANT TO
GO RIGHT NOW?

346
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:24,554
'CAUSE I'LL TAKE YOU
RIGHT NOW, BUDDY.

347
00:13:24,596 --> 00:13:26,306
YOU WANT TO GO?

348
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:28,015
OH, FINE.

349
00:13:29,934 --> 00:13:31,519
READY?

350
00:13:31,561 --> 00:13:32,979
WRESTLE.

351
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:39,193
OKAY, OKAY.
YOU KNOW WHAT?

352
00:13:39,235 --> 00:13:40,819
UM, ACTUALLY,
THAT'S GREAT.

353
00:13:40,861 --> 00:13:42,405
THAT HELPS A
LOT. THANKS.

354
00:13:47,368 --> 00:13:50,497
GUYS, COME ON. LET'S GO.
THE PUCK DROPS IN 20 MINUTES.

355
00:13:50,538 --> 00:13:52,248
JOEY'S NOT GOING.

356
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:54,751
I DIDN'T FINISH
MY FIVE PAGES.

357
00:13:54,793 --> 00:13:57,712
WELL, WHY CAN'T YOU
FINISH THEM TOMORROW?

358
00:13:57,754 --> 00:14:00,507
BECAUSE TOMORROW
HE'S REDOING YESTERDAY'S PAGES.

359
00:14:00,548 --> 00:14:04,552
AND YESTERDAY'S PAGES
DID NOT REFLECT MY BEST WORK.

360
00:14:04,594 --> 00:14:06,387
WHY DON'T YOU CUT HIM
A LITTLE SLACK, OKAY?

361
00:14:06,429 --> 00:14:09,015
MAYBE IF HE RELAXES A LITTLE
BIT, HE'LL GET SOME WORK DONE.

362
00:14:09,056 --> 00:14:10,684
I THINK HE'S BEEN
RELAXING ENOUGH

363
00:14:10,725 --> 00:14:13,936
THANKS TO YOU
AND FIREBALL.

364
00:14:15,313 --> 00:14:17,106
DUDE, IF YOU THINK
FIREBALL'S RELAXING

365
00:14:17,148 --> 00:14:18,857
YOU OBVIOUSLY HAVE NEVER PLAYED.

366
00:14:18,899 --> 00:14:20,985
THE ONLY REASON
YOU ARE DOING THIS TO JOEY

367
00:14:21,027 --> 00:14:22,945
IS BECAUSE YOU ARE BORED, OKAY?

368
00:14:22,987 --> 00:14:24,905
IT'S NOT HIS FAULT
YOU'RE UNEMPLOYED.

369
00:14:24,947 --> 00:14:26,240
I AM NOT UNEMPLOYED.

370
00:14:26,282 --> 00:14:27,742
I'M ON SABBATICAL.

371
00:14:27,784 --> 00:14:30,411
COME ON, LOOK, GUYS.
DON'T FIGHT.

372
00:14:30,453 --> 00:14:34,081
AND THE REASON I'M DOING THIS
IS BECAUSE I AM JOEY'S FRIEND

373
00:14:34,123 --> 00:14:37,251
AND IF YOU WERE A GOOD FRIEND,
YOU'D BE DOING THE SAME THING.

374
00:14:37,293 --> 00:14:39,713
SO BEING A GOOD
FRIEND MEANS ACTING
LIKE A TOTAL JERK.

375
00:14:39,754 --> 00:14:42,089
IF IT DOES, THEN YOU'RE
AN AMAZING FRIEND OF MINE.

376
00:14:42,131 --> 00:14:43,383
Joey:
HEY, GUYS, HEY.

377
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:44,843
HOW ABOUT WE SETTLE THIS

378
00:14:44,884 --> 00:14:46,803
OVER A FRIENDLY
GAME OF FIREBALL? HUH?

379
00:14:46,845 --> 00:14:48,596
I'LL GO UNHOOK THE
SMOKE DETECTORS.

380
00:14:48,638 --> 00:14:50,431
HOW ABOUT WE SETTLE THIS
RIGHT NOW?

381
00:14:50,473 --> 00:14:52,475
( gasps )

382
00:14:52,517 --> 00:14:55,311
THERE. NOW NO ONE'S GOING
TO THE GAME.

383
00:14:55,353 --> 00:14:57,063
I PAID FOR THOSE TICKETS.

384
00:14:57,104 --> 00:14:59,315
NO, YOU DIDN'T.
YOU SAID YOU WOULD,
BUT YOU NEVER DID.

385
00:14:59,357 --> 00:15:00,483
OH, YEAH.

386
00:15:00,525 --> 00:15:01,860
( goofy laughing )

387
00:15:07,490 --> 00:15:10,785
SO, WE FINALLY GET
TO THE TOP OF THE MOUNTAIN

388
00:15:10,827 --> 00:15:13,538
AND AIRHEAD HERE
FORGETS THE CAMERA.

389
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:17,500
WELL, YOU KNOW, THAT
SAME THING HAPPENED
TO ME ONE TIME.

390
00:15:17,542 --> 00:15:20,169
WHEN DID THAT
HAPPEN TO YOU?

391
00:15:20,211 --> 00:15:21,504
DON'T YOU REMEMBER?

392
00:15:21,546 --> 00:15:22,921
WE WERE JOGGING
IN THE PARK

393
00:15:22,963 --> 00:15:24,465
WE SAW THAT
REALLY PRETTY BIRD

394
00:15:24,507 --> 00:15:26,050
AND I WANTED
TO TAKE A PICTURE

395
00:15:26,092 --> 00:15:27,761
BUT I DIDN'T HAVE
MY CAMERA.

396
00:15:27,802 --> 00:15:31,180
OKAY. FIRST OF ALL,
CHASING THE CHURRO
GUY IS NOT JOGGING.

397
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:34,100
OH, THIS IS SO GOOD.

398
00:15:34,141 --> 00:15:35,894
YOU HAVE GOT TO TRY IT.

399
00:15:42,233 --> 00:15:44,235
THAT IS GOOD.

400
00:15:46,863 --> 00:15:49,156
OH. DAMN.
I GOT IT ON MY PANTS.

401
00:15:49,198 --> 00:15:51,409
HERE. I'LL GET IT.

402
00:15:57,832 --> 00:15:59,208
WE BETTER TAKE
THESE OFF UPSTAIRS

403
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:00,877
OR THAT STAIN'S
GOING TO SET.

404
00:16:00,919 --> 00:16:03,254
I WANT TO WEAR THESE PANTS
ON OUR DATE TONIGHT.

405
00:16:03,296 --> 00:16:06,006
OH, GREAT.

406
00:16:06,048 --> 00:16:07,508
OKAY. BYE.

407
00:16:07,550 --> 00:16:09,343
OH, MY GOD...

408
00:16:09,385 --> 00:16:11,053
THAT WAS UNBELIEVABLE.

409
00:16:11,095 --> 00:16:12,555
OKAY, SEE? I TOLD YOU.

410
00:16:12,597 --> 00:16:14,098
YEAH, WOW... SORRY, RACH.

411
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:16,142
I DON'T BELIEVE
THEY'RE BROTHER AND SISTER.

412
00:16:16,183 --> 00:16:17,727
THEY'RE BROTHER AND SISTER?!

413
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:21,439
( bell ringing )

414
00:16:29,864 --> 00:16:32,032
OH! WAIT A MINUTE.
OPEN YOUR HAND.

415
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:34,368
LET ME TAKE A LOOK.

416
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:36,370
QUARTER, DIME, LINT.

417
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:38,706
NOT INTERESTED IN THAT.

418
00:16:38,748 --> 00:16:40,667
WHAT'S THIS,
A CANADIAN COIN?

419
00:16:40,708 --> 00:16:42,042
GET OUT OF HERE!

420
00:16:42,084 --> 00:16:44,879
OH, MY GOSH.

421
00:16:46,130 --> 00:16:48,549
WHOA! NO DRINKS
NEAR THE BUCKET.

422
00:16:48,591 --> 00:16:49,884
SET IT DOWN OVER THERE

423
00:16:49,926 --> 00:16:51,594
AND THEN YOU CAN
MAKE A CONTRIBUTION.

424
00:16:51,636 --> 00:16:56,265
AND YOU LEAVE THE
"HURT BUNNY" LOOK
OVER THERE, TOO.

425
00:16:56,307 --> 00:16:57,976
OH, HI, BOB.

426
00:16:58,016 --> 00:17:02,188
I THOUGHT I TOLD YOU
TO GET OUT OF HERE!

427
00:17:02,229 --> 00:17:04,732
UH, PHOEBE,
WE'VE BEEN GETTING COMPLAINTS

428
00:17:04,774 --> 00:17:08,235
AND, UH, WE'RE GOING TO MOVE YOU
TO A LESS HIGH-PROFILE SPOT.

429
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:09,570
WHAT?

430
00:17:09,612 --> 00:17:11,531
UH, GINGER'S GOING TO
TAKE OVER THIS CORNER.

431
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:14,032
THAT CHICK CAN'T
HANDLE MY CORNER.

432
00:17:14,074 --> 00:17:17,704
LOOK, EITHER YOU
LEAVE OR WE REMOVE YOU.

433
00:17:17,745 --> 00:17:19,288
FINE.

434
00:17:24,293 --> 00:17:27,254
ALL RIGHT. I'LL
GIVE YOU ONE POINTER.

435
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:28,882
LOOK AT FOR THAT BITCH.

436
00:17:34,012 --> 00:17:35,763
( knocking )

437
00:17:38,892 --> 00:17:41,728
OH. HI, RACH.
I THOUGHT WE SAID 7:00.

438
00:17:41,769 --> 00:17:44,062
YEAH. YOU KNOW WHAT?
UH, LET'S SKIP IT.

439
00:17:44,104 --> 00:17:45,982
WHAT? WHY?

440
00:17:46,024 --> 00:17:50,987
UM... YOU AND YOUR
SISTER SEEM TO HAVE
A VERY SPECIAL BOND.

441
00:17:51,029 --> 00:17:54,448
OH, GREAT.
THAT SPECIAL BOND AGAIN.

442
00:17:54,490 --> 00:17:57,451
WHY DO WOMEN HAVE
SUCH A PROBLEM
WITH THE FACT

443
00:17:57,493 --> 00:17:59,746
THAT I'M CLOSE
WITH MY SISTER?

444
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:01,330
WELL... OKAY, LOOK.

445
00:18:01,372 --> 00:18:03,499
LISTEN... I DON'T
KNOW WHAT'S GOING
ON HERE, BUT...

446
00:18:03,541 --> 00:18:05,001
DO YOU HAVE BROTHERS?

447
00:18:05,043 --> 00:18:06,586
NO. I HAVE TWO SISTERS.

448
00:18:06,627 --> 00:18:09,380
ONE OF THEM ACTUALLY HAS
A VERY MASCULINE ENERGY.

449
00:18:09,422 --> 00:18:10,882
ARE YOU CLOSE WITH THEM?

450
00:18:10,924 --> 00:18:13,300
NO, NO. THEY'RE NOT
VERY NICE PEOPLE.

451
00:18:13,342 --> 00:18:14,635
COME HERE.

452
00:18:14,677 --> 00:18:16,763
LISTEN. I REALLY
LIKE YOU, OKAY?

453
00:18:16,804 --> 00:18:18,973
I THINK THIS COULD
GO SOMEWHERE.

454
00:18:19,015 --> 00:18:20,725
SO WHAT IF I'M CLOSE
TO MY FAMILY?

455
00:18:20,767 --> 00:18:22,685
YOU GOING TO LET THAT
STAND IN THE WAY OF US?

456
00:18:22,727 --> 00:18:24,854
WELL... I DON'T KNOW.

457
00:18:24,896 --> 00:18:28,190
WHEN YOU PUT IT THAT
WAY, YOU KNOW...

458
00:18:28,232 --> 00:18:31,903
DANNY, HURRY UP.
THE BATH'S GETTING COLD.

459
00:18:34,948 --> 00:18:35,907
WHAT?

460
00:18:35,949 --> 00:18:37,491
YEAH. I'LL SEE YOU LATER.

461
00:18:41,996 --> 00:18:44,707
OH, HEY. THERE'S
SOME KIDS PLAYING
IN THE STREET.

462
00:18:44,749 --> 00:18:46,375
YOU WANT TO
GO DOWN THERE

463
00:18:46,417 --> 00:18:48,628
GIVE THEM A PROJECT,
RUIN THEIR DAY?

464
00:18:48,669 --> 00:18:50,337
HEY, IF THEY HAVE A BALL

465
00:18:50,379 --> 00:18:52,715
MAYBE YOU COULD STICK
RAZOR BLADES IN IT

466
00:18:52,757 --> 00:18:55,802
AND TEACH THEM A NEW GAME--
"GOING TO NEED STITCHES" BALL.

467
00:18:57,261 --> 00:18:59,764
HEY, GUYS. I WAS
AT THE LIBRARY ALL MORNING

468
00:18:59,806 --> 00:19:02,558
AND I ALREADY
FINISHED MY FIVE
PAGES FOR TODAY.

469
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:07,063
GREAT. NOW WE CAN
GO TO THE RANGER
GAME LAST NIGHT.

470
00:19:07,105 --> 00:19:10,775
NO, DUDE.
ROSS TORE UP THE TICKETS.

471
00:19:14,737 --> 00:19:17,573
I GUESS WHEN YOU DON'T HAVE
SO MANY DISTRACTIONS

472
00:19:17,615 --> 00:19:19,951
IT'S EASIER FOR YOU
TO FOCUS, HUH?

473
00:19:19,993 --> 00:19:22,120
YEAH, OR ALSO,
WHEN YOU DON'T HAVE SOMEBODY

474
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:24,622
BREATHING DOWN YOUR NECK
ALL THE LIVELONG DAY!

475
00:19:26,624 --> 00:19:28,835
WELL... THAT'S FINE,
BUT THE IMPORTANT THING IS

476
00:19:28,876 --> 00:19:30,878
I FINISHED IT
AND I THINK IT'S REALLY GOOD

477
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:32,672
BUT YOU KNOW
WHAT WOULD REALLY HELP ME

478
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:35,424
IS IF I COULD HEAR IT, SO
WOULD YOU GUYS READ IT FOR ME?

479
00:19:35,466 --> 00:19:37,259
ALL RIGHT.

480
00:19:37,301 --> 00:19:39,386
ALL RIGHT.

481
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:40,888
OKAY.

482
00:19:40,930 --> 00:19:44,183
IT'S A TYPICAL NEW
YORK CITY APARTMENT--

483
00:19:44,224 --> 00:19:47,061
TWO GUYS ARE
HANGING OUT. ROSS?

484
00:19:49,772 --> 00:19:51,565
HEY, MAN.

485
00:19:51,607 --> 00:19:54,568
WHAT IS UP?

486
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:57,404
ABOUT YESTERDAY,
I WAS REALLY WRONG.

487
00:19:57,446 --> 00:19:59,073
I AM SORRY.

488
00:19:59,115 --> 00:20:02,910
NO, IT WAS ME. I'M
SORRY. I OVERREACTED.

489
00:20:02,952 --> 00:20:05,204
MAYBE IT WAS BOTH OF US

490
00:20:05,245 --> 00:20:08,499
BUT WE HAD
OUR BEST FRIEND'S INTER...

491
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:14,922
BUT WE HAD OUR BEST FRIEND'S
INTEREST AT HEART.

492
00:20:14,964 --> 00:20:18,092
COULD I BE MORE SORRY?

493
00:20:22,304 --> 00:20:24,473
I DON'T KNOW.

494
00:20:24,515 --> 00:20:29,603
I AM ONE SORRY...
POLONTOLOGIST...

495
00:20:32,523 --> 00:20:35,151
ALL RIGHT, JOEY.
WE-WE GET IT.

496
00:20:35,193 --> 00:20:36,485
I'M SORRY.

497
00:20:36,527 --> 00:20:37,904
I'M SORRY, TOO.

498
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:39,279
OH, NO. NO, NO. KEEP READING.

499
00:20:39,321 --> 00:20:41,032
THE GOOD PART'S COMING UP.
KEEP GOING.

500
00:20:43,367 --> 00:20:46,537
I AM SORRY, CHANDLER.

501
00:20:46,579 --> 00:20:48,581
I AM SORRY, ROSS.

502
00:20:51,042 --> 00:20:53,044
A HANDSOME
MAN ENTERS.

503
00:20:54,294 --> 00:20:57,255
HEY... HOW'S IT
GOING, GUYS?

504
00:20:57,297 --> 00:20:58,758
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT YOU TWO ARE
TALKING ABOUT

505
00:20:58,799 --> 00:21:01,219
BUT I WOULD JUST
LIKE TO SAY THANKS
TO BOTH OF YOU.

506
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:05,389
YOU-- YOU WOULDN'T LET
ME GIVE UP ON MYSELF

507
00:21:05,431 --> 00:21:10,144
AND YOU-- WELL, YOU
CO-CREATED FIREBALL.

508
00:21:10,186 --> 00:21:11,687
THE END.

509
00:21:13,064 --> 00:21:15,482
THIS TOOK YOU ALL DAY?

510
00:21:15,524 --> 00:21:17,693
NO, NO. THIS ONLY
TOOK FIVE MINUTES.

511
00:21:17,735 --> 00:21:19,403
I SPENT THE
REST OF THE DAY

512
00:21:19,445 --> 00:21:22,198
COMING UP WITH NEW,
ULTIMATE FIREBALL.

513
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:24,242
( crazed laughing )

514
00:21:29,329 --> 00:21:30,414
IT'S A TYPICAL

515
00:21:30,456 --> 00:21:32,125
NEW YORK CITY APARTMENT.

516
00:21:32,166 --> 00:21:35,211
TWO GIRLS ARE JUST HANGING OUT.

517
00:21:35,253 --> 00:21:37,671
HI. HOW'RE YOU
DOING, KELLY?

518
00:21:37,713 --> 00:21:39,673
I'M DOING JUST FINE.

519
00:21:39,715 --> 00:21:42,509
GOD, TIFFANY,
YOU SMELL SO GREAT.

520
00:21:44,470 --> 00:21:46,180
IT'S MY NEW PERFUME.

521
00:21:46,222 --> 00:21:48,015
WHY DON'T YOU
COME CLOSER

522
00:21:48,057 --> 00:21:50,726
WHERE YOU CAN REALLY
APPRECIATE IT?

523
00:21:53,146 --> 00:21:54,730
OH, YOU KNOW, JOEY,
YOU ARE SICK.

524
00:21:54,772 --> 00:21:55,898
THIS IS DISGUSTING.

525
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:57,441
I'M NOT READING THIS.

526
00:21:57,483 --> 00:22:01,279
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT. THE HANDSOME
MAN WAS ABOUT TO ENTER!

527
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:03,322
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

